Z||000031||Smoooooth GT||06-04-2001||01:01 AM||||Songman...   Cool, I'll try to find that post...  Maybe ..  maybe not... lol<BR>As, far as my exhaust is concerned, I have a 80 series Flowmaster. I have the exhaust exiting curved straight downward just in frint of the trunk. BUT....  That IS a very good idea. I'll keep that in mind. That is something that I could do at a later time.<BR>HEY....  KEEP THE GREAT IDEA'S COMING,<BR>I am going inthe morning to get the form for special plates..  they will read. SMOOTH<BR>Thank's ...  Steve<P>------------------<BR>aka..FieroSEt<BR>Fiero_87GT@yahoo.com<BR>cell.. 903 445 0849<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_6.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000032||Smoooooth GT||06-04-2001||01:07 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fyerstarter:<BR><B>Dood!!! I love it! I've always wanted to do that but looked like so much work. You gotta shave the doorhandles. Please keep us posted.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Fyerstarter...  LOL  It is alot of work , especially concidering this is my FIRST shot at doing anykind of body work at all!!<BR>This car started out as being a replacment for my totalled 87GT..This is a 86SE..  WAS A 86 SE..lol  I replaced the motor,tran's,GT conversion,Flowmaster,etc... I can't wait until I'm finished. I hope to get to Daytona next year at least.  Keep the idea's coming everybody.                 Steve<P>------------------<BR>aka..FieroSEt<BR>Fiero_87GT@yahoo.com<BR>cell.. 903 445 0849<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_6.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000033||sqoach||06-04-2001||02:02 AM||||Looking good! I want to do something like this, but it won't be as cool now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Here's a couple of ideas. Take off the black drip rails, or whatever they're called, above the windows. Try to make the front turn signals, and back reflectors flush to the fascia. Or even try to do DXR_DAD's back-up light mod in the rear fascia. Or hell, eliminate the back ones completely. Here's another idea, but probably not a good one. Smooth out the front fascia "mouth." This wouldn't be a good idea though, cuz it wouldn't get air to the radiator well at all. Actually, just scratch that idea. And I'm sure you shaved all the emblems  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach2.JPG">   <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||10
Z||000034||Smoooooth GT||06-04-2001||03:04 AM||||sqoach...  Thanks for the good comment's. That is what is keeping this project fresh and exciting for me...<BR>As afr as the drip rail's are concerned... This car was a 86SE so the drip rail's stop at the end of the roof panel...<BR>The rear fascia is smooooth too. I fiberglassed in the exhaust outlet's..  I'm thinking about running the exhaust out from just behind the door's..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>I'm going to put backup light's in where the reflector's are now.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pass_rear_fascia_smooth.JPG"> <BR>Keep the idea's coming...  Steve<P>------------------<BR>aka..FieroSEt<BR>Fiero_87GT@yahoo.com<BR>cell.. 903 445 0849<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_6.JPG"> ||||reg||1
